  "bodyTypst": "A particle moves in the $x y$-plane so that its position at any time $t \\, 0 <= t <= pi$, is given by $x(t)= frac(t^(2),2)- ln(1 + t)$ and $y(t)= 3 sin t$.\n\n(a) Sketch the path of the particle in the $x y$-plane below. Indicate the direction of motion along the path.\n\n#image(\"/imgs/ap-calc-bc-1999-frq-01-diagram-01.jpg\", width: 65%)\n\n(b) At what time $t \\, 0 <= t <= pi$, does $x(t)$ attain its minimum value? What is the position $(x(t)\\, y(t))$ of the particle at this time?\n\n(c) At what time $t \\, 0 < t < pi$, is the particle on the $y$-axis? Find the speed and the acceleration vector of the particle at this time.",
